      "role": "user",
      "content": "I'm currently troubleshooting a persistent 403 Forbidden error occurring during the authentication handshake on our enterprise deployment. We've already verified that the client-side cache is clear and the session cookies are being passed correctly. Could you provide a detailed breakdown of the typical permission hierarchies in your system that might trigger a 403, specifically regarding JWT validation and CORS policy misconfigurations? I need to cross-reference these with our current Nginx ingress controller settings.",
