      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In a typical JWT-based system, permission hierarchies are defined by the roles assigned to users. Here's a breakdown: \n\n1. **Token validation:** The server verifies the issued-at, expiration, and signature of the JWT. \n2. **Role-based access control:** The server checks the user's role against a set of predefined roles with associated permissions. If the role is not recognized or doesn't match a required role, a 403 error is returned.\n\nCommon CORS policy misconfigurations that might trigger 403s include:\n\n1. Missing or incorrect allow-origin header\n2. Inconsistent origin headers between client and server\n3. Incorrect content-security-policy (CSP)\n\nWhen troubleshooting, you can check your Nginx ingress controller configuration to ensure it includes:\n\n1. Allow-origin headers for external clients\n2. CORS headers for upstream servers\n3. CSP to define allowed sources",
